                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesForEquivariantBundles"} For equivariant bundles
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong classifying space
            for some sort of data is (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of) a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to A
            correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of that kind of data “parameterized” over suitable base spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %blockquote
            %p
              Beware the similarity with but distinction to
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              match, but that the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-groupoid
              of (structured) maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{A}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+infinity-groupoids"} equivalent
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-groupoid
              of the given kind of data on a suitable stack
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              (Moduli stacks, in turn – with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stacks"} stacks
              understood in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+homotopy+theory"} directed
              generality of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaves"} 2-sheaves
              etc. — subsume yet more general kinds of “universes”. For instance the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
              may be understood as exhibiting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              as the moduli object for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              %em spaces
              over moduli stacks is to be more coarse, and hence more informative concerning equivalence classes.)
          %p
            The classical examples of classifying spaces (both historically and by prevalence of their applications) are traditionally denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            and constructed as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+constructions"} bar constructions
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+realization+of+simplicial+topological+spaces"} topological realizations
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerves"} nerves
            of suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            (hence the “data” above being:
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsors"} torsors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi BG
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to BG
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            over suitable base spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p This case is often understood by default when referring to “classifying spaces”.
          %p
            But every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+homotopy+type"} connected homotopy type
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak equivalently
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            for
            %em some
            topological group and other objects than just ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            may be classified by these spaces.
          %p
            For example,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spaces"} Eilenberg-MacLane spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(G,n)
            have the property that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of maps into them are in bijection with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} cohomology groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ;
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n(-;G)
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            for
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            this situation overlaps with the previous one classifying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            and with due care, one may think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(G,n)
            as classifying certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+infinity-bundles"}
              principal
              = succeed "-bundles" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"}> bundle gerbes
            ”, “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+2-gerbes"}> bundle 2-gerbes
            ”, etc.).
          %p
            In joint generalization of these two situations, there are classifying spaces for
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundles"} principal 2-bundles
            for non-abelian topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groups"} 2-groups
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            In fact, one may understand
            %em any
            connected space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            as being the classifying space for generalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ;
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^1(-;\Omega A)
            with coefficients in the loop
            = succeed "-group" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega A
          %p
            Traditionally familiar (in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology+theories"} Whitehead-generalized cohomology theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
            says that their classifying spaces are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-loop+spaces"} infinite-loop spaces
            which, as the degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            ranges, organize into sequences of spaces called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#for_principal_bundles For principal bundles
          %blockquote
            %p
              A good account is in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#RudolfSchmidt17"} Rudolf &amp; Schmidt 17, Sec. 3, esp. Thm. 3.5.1 &amp; Prop. 3.6.2
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            there is a classifying space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            for topological
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            any sufficiently nice topological space there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Bund
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G Bund(X)_0 \simeq \pi_0 Top(X, B G)
          %p
            between the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            classes of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and the set of
            = succeed "-classes" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to B G
          %p This space may be constructed as follows:
          %p
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G \in Top^{\Delta^{op}}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+topological+space"} simplicial topological space
            obtained as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of the one-object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groupoid"} topological groupoid
            associated to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %mo ×
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\mathbf{B}G)_n = G^{\times n}
          %p
            whose face maps are induced by the product operation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and whose degeneracy maps are induced from the unit map.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+simplicial+topological+group"} well-pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+simplicial+topological+spaces"} geometric realization of simplicial topological spaces
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a model for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of the classifying space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B G \simeq \vert \mathbf{B}G\vert
                  \\,.
          %p
            For more details on this construction see the section
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+simplicial+topological+spaces#ClassifyingSpaces"} classifying spaces
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+simplicial+topological+spaces"} geometric realization of simplicial topological spaces
          %p
            As discussed there, too, this construction generalizes to more general
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+topological+group"} simplicial topological group
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
          %p
            %br/
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
