                    (E O(n+1))/O(n+1)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The claim in then follows since (
              %a{:href => "coset#nSphereAsCosetSpace"}> this exmpl.
              )
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    O(n+1)/O(n) \simeq S^n
                    \\,.
            %p
              The argument for the complex case is of the same form, concluding now with the identification (
              %a{:href => "unitary+group#nSphereAsUnitaryCosetSpace"}> this exmpl.
              )
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U(n+1)/U(n) \simeq S^{2n+1}
                    \\,.
          %h4#classification_of_bundles Classification of bundles
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact topological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal principal bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E O(n) \to B O(n)
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EOn"}
              along
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to B O(n)
              establishes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi iso
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ↦
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mi E
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Bund
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [X, B O(n)]
                    \\underoverset{iso}{f \mapsto f^\ast E O(n)}{\longrightarrow}
                    O(n) Bund/_\sim
            %p
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
              of functions from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BO%28n%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O(n)
              and isomorphism classes of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            A full proof is spelled out in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Hatcher"} Hatcher, section 1.2, theorem 1.16
          %h3#for_symmetric_principal_bundles For symmetric principal bundles
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %em unordered
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fadell%27s+configuration+space"} Fadell's configuration space
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                points in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\infty
                is a model for the classifying space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \Sigma(n)
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(n)
            %li
              %p
                the
                %em ordered
                configuration space of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                points, equipped with the canonical
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(n)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(n)
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+bundle"} universal principal bundle
          %h3#for_crossed_complexes For crossed complexes
          %p
            We discuss here classifying spaces of
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
          %p The notion of classifying space should be regarded in general terms as giving a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi algebraic
                  %mi data
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi topological
                  %mi data
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B} :(algebraic data) \to (topological data).
          %p
            Composition with a forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi topological
                  %mi data
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi topological
                  %mi spaces
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: (topological data) \to (topological spaces)
            gives a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ξ
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi topological
                  %mi data
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi algebraic
                  %mi data
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi: (topological data) \to (algebraic data)
          %p such that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ξ
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi ℬ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi \circ \mathcal{B}
                is equivalent to the identity;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ξ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi
                preserves certain colimits (Generalised
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/van+Kampen+theorem"} van Kampen theorem
            %li
              %p
                there are notions of homotopy for both types of data leading to a bijection of homotopy classes for some
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Ξ
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,U\mathcal{B}C] \cong [\Xi X_*, C].
          %p
            This happens for the algebraic data of crossed complexes and the topological data of filtered spaces, when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a CW-complex, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ξ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi
            is the fundamental crossed complex of a filtered space. Thus in this case the classifying space does classify homotopy classes of maps, and more work is needed to sort out the data over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            which this classifies (gerbes?).
          %p
            However
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}C
            is in this case defined by a nerve construction which generalises that for groupoids, and can also be applied to topological crossed crossed complexes, giving a simplicial space.
          %p
            Some such constructions arise from generalisations of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            one obtains a simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Nerve
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Nerve(C)
            which in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Crs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo *
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Crs(\Pi(\Delta^n_*),C)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}C
            of this is canonically filtered by the skeleta of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            is really a functor to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+spaces"} filtered spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            which goes in the opposite direction. But note that there is a different filtration of the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}C
            since it is a CW-complex, and so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            of this filtration gives a free crossed complex.
          %p
            Special cases of crossed complexes are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
          %p A crossed module is equivalent to a category object in groups, and so a nerve of this can be constructed as a bisimplicial set. The geometric realisation of this is naturally bifiltered, in several ways!
          %p
            In considering what is desirable for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+infinity-groupoid"} fundamental infinity-groupoid
            one should bring the notion of classifying space, and its inherited structure, into account.
          %h3#ForSimplicialGroups For simplicial groups
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+classifying+space"} simplicial classifying space
            = succeed "-construction" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{W}(-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object in an (∞,1)-category
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+loop+groupoid"} Dwyer-Kan loop groupoid
            functor and induces an equivalence of homotopy categories between that of simplicial sets and that of simplicially enriched groupoids. The simplicial sets here are playing the role of ‘topological data’.
          %h2#properties_2 Properties
          %h3#for_classical_lie_groups For classical Lie groups
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(n)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
            in real/complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          #CWComplexStructure.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              The real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmannians"} Grassmannians
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gr_n(\mathbb{R}^k)
              and the complex Grassmannians
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gr_n(\mathbb{C}^k)
              admit the structure of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Gr_n(\mathbb{R}^k)
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Gr_n(\mathbb{R}^{k+1})
            %p
              are subcomplex incusion (hence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
              inclusions).
            %p Accordingly there is an induced CW-complex structure on the classifying space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B O(n) \simeq \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_k Gr_n(\mathbb{R}^k)
                    \\,.
          %p
            A proof is spelled out in (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher"}> Hatcher, section 1.2 (pages 31-34)
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              The classifying spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BO%28n%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O(n)
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+spaces"} paracompact spaces
          %p
            An early source of this statement is (
            %a{:href => "#CartanSchwartz63"}> Cartan-Schwartz 63, exposé 5
            ). It follows for instance by prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CWComplexStructure"}
            the fact that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            is paracompact.
          %h3#cohomology Cohomology
          %div
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    (
